  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Using the common logarithm and scientific notation, evaluate each of the following correct to three significant figures:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(1.24\\times10^3)\\times(4.13\\times10^4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5.12\\times10^7$",
          "worked": "Let $A=(1.24\\times10^3)(4.13\\times10^4)$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=\\log_{10}1.24+\\log_{10}4.13+7\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx0.0934+0.6160+7\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx7.7094.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.7094}\\times10^7\\approx5.12\\times10^7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(2.46\\times10^3)\\times(1.34\\times10^4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.30\\times10^7$",
          "worked": "Let $A=(2.46\\times10^3)(1.34\\times10^4)$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=\\log_{10}2.46+\\log_{10}1.34+7\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx0.3909+0.1271+7\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx7.5180.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.5180}\\times10^7\\approx3.30\\times10^7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(8.24\\times10^4)\\times(4.76\\times10^5)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.92\\times10^{10}$",
          "worked": "Let $A=(8.24\\times10^4)(4.76\\times10^5)$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=\\log_{10}8.24+\\log_{10}4.76+9\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx0.9159+0.6776+9\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx10.5935.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.5935}\\times10^{10}\\approx3.92\\times10^{10}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(5.67\\times10^3)\\times(8.88\\times10^4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5.03\\times10^8$",
          "worked": "Let $A=(5.67\\times10^3)(8.88\\times10^4)$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=\\log_{10}5.67+\\log_{10}8.88+7\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx0.7536+0.9484+7\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx8.7020.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.7020}\\times10^8\\approx5.03\\times10^8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(3.05\\times10^{-3})\\times(3.13\\times10^7)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$9.55\\times10^4$",
          "worked": "Let $A=(3.05\\times10^{-3})(3.13\\times10^7)$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=\\log_{10}3.05+\\log_{10}3.13+4\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx0.4843+0.4955+4\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx4.9798.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.9798}\\times10^4\\approx9.55\\times10^4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$(3.25\\times10^{-3})\\times(3.15\\times10^5)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.02\\times10^3$",
          "worked": "Let $A=(3.25\\times10^{-3})(3.15\\times10^5)$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=\\log_{10}3.25+\\log_{10}3.15+2\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx0.5119+0.4983+2\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx3.0102.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.0102}\\times10^3\\approx1.02\\times10^3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$3^{33}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5.56\\times10^{15}$",
          "worked": "Retaining extra logarithm precision,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(3^{33})&=33\\log_{10}3\\\\\\log_{10}(3^{33})&\\approx33(0.4771212547)\\\\\\log_{10}(3^{33})&\\approx15.7450014.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $3^{33}\\approx10^{0.7450014}\\times10^{15}\\approx5.56\\times10^{15}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$44^{44}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2.05\\times10^{72}$",
          "worked": "Write $44=4.4\\times10$. Retaining extra logarithm precision,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(44^{44})&=44(\\log_{10}4.4+1)\\\\\\log_{10}(44^{44})&\\approx44(0.6434526765+1)\\\\\\log_{10}(44^{44})&\\approx72.3119178.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $44^{44}\\approx10^{0.3119178}\\times10^{72}\\approx2.05\\times10^{72}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{1.24\\times10^6}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.11\\times10^3$",
          "worked": "Let $A=\\sqrt{1.24\\times10^6}$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=\\frac12(\\log_{10}1.24+6)\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx\\frac12(0.0934+6)\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx3.0467.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.0467}\\times10^3\\approx1.11\\times10^3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt[3]{3.14\\times10^9}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.46\\times10^3$",
          "worked": "Let $A=\\sqrt[3]{3.14\\times10^9}$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=\\frac13(\\log_{10}3.14+9)\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx\\frac13(0.4969+9)\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx3.1656333.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.1656333}\\times10^3\\approx1.46\\times10^3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$(2.14\\times10^3)^2\\times(4.17\\times10^4)^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.32\\times10^{20}$\n\nMultiply each common logarithm by its power, add, then reverse the logarithm.",
          "worked": "Let $A=(2.14\\times10^3)^2(4.17\\times10^4)^3$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=2(\\log_{10}2.14+3)+3(\\log_{10}4.17+4)\\\\\\log_{10}A&=2\\log_{10}2.14+3\\log_{10}4.17+18\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx2(0.3304)+3(0.6201)+18\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx20.5211.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.5211}\\times10^{20}\\approx3.32\\times10^{20}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q6-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$(1.64\\times10^3)^5\\times(6.54\\times10^{-4})^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5.07\\times10^9$\n\nMultiply each common logarithm by its power, add, then reverse the logarithm.",
          "worked": "Let $A=(1.64\\times10^3)^5(6.54\\times10^{-4})^2$. Using the logarithm table,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}A&=5(\\log_{10}1.64+3)+2(\\log_{10}6.54-4)\\\\\\log_{10}A&=5\\log_{10}1.64+2\\log_{10}6.54+7\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx5(0.2148)+2(0.8156)+7\\\\\\log_{10}A&\\approx9.7052.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $A\\approx10^{0.7052}\\times10^9\\approx5.07\\times10^9$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
